# Harness Adapters

¶ - Where each supported harness reads global rules, skills and hooks, and what the installer writes there.

document:
  id: task.adapters@1
  version: 2.2.0
  status: active
  scope: claude_code, codex, antigravity, cline

¶ 1 — Shared Layout

```text
kernel_home ~/.task # one copy of scripts, docs, grammar, skills and kernel.config.json for every harness
policy kernel/policy.tdsl.md rendered once -> {{KERNEL_HOME}}/policy.tdsl.md, then placed per harness below
skills kernel/skills/* copied into each harness skill directory, {{KERNEL_HOME}} resolved
hooks the harness hook script is copied into {{KERNEL_HOME}}/scripts/ so it resolves docs and gates from the kernel
existing_file -> back up to {{KERNEL_HOME}}/backups/<timestamp>/ before writing; never discard operator content
```

¶ 2 — Claude Code

```text
policy ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md # merge: keep operator content, insert the policy between `<!-- task:begin -->` and `<!-- task:end -->`
skills ~/.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md
hooks merge adapters/claude/settings.hooks.json into ~/.claude/settings.json `hooks`
hook_script adapters/claude/claude_hook.py -> {{KERNEL_HOME}}/scripts/claude_hook.py
enforcement mechanical: the PreToolUse hook runs the gate before a .task write and injects engineering.tdsl
```

¶ 3 — Codex

```text
policy ~/.codex/AGENTS.md # same merge markers; AGENTS.override.md, when present, wins over it
  size AGENTS.md is truncated past 32 KiB
skills ~/.codex/skills/<name>/SKILL.md # global; project skills live in .agents/skills/
hooks merge adapters/codex/hooks.json into ~/.codex/hooks.json # on by default; inline [hooks] in config.toml also valid
hook_script adapters/codex/codex_hook.py -> {{KERNEL_HOME}}/scripts/codex_hook.py
enforcement mechanical on apply_patch; delegation contract injected on SubagentStart
source developers.openai.com/codex/config-reference, verified 2026-11-02
```

¶ 4 — Antigravity

```text
policy ~/.gemini/GEMINI.md # same merge markers; keep the file under ~12000 characters
  note Gemini CLI reads the same file; one block serves both
  alt ~/.gemini/AGENTS.md, ~/.gemini/config/GEMINI.md, ~/.gemini/config/rules/*.md (YAML frontmatter)
skills ~/.gemini/config/skills/<name>/SKILL.md # shared by every Antigravity product
  also ~/.gemini/antigravity/skills (IDE) and ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/skills (CLI) when present
  workspace skills live in .agents/skills/
hooks ~/.gemini/config/hooks.json exists; the kernel ships no adapter yet -> instruction-driven, as policy ¶11 instructs
size_guard rendered policy > 12000 chars -> keep the operator's own ¶1-¶3 and place kernel ¶4 onward
source antigravity.google/docs/rules, antigravity.google/docs/cli/gcli-migration, verified 2026-11-02
```

¶ 5 — Cline

```text
policy ~/Documents/Cline/Rules/task-policy.md # still discovered for compatibility; newer builds also read ~/.cline/rules
skills ~/.cline/skills/<name>/SKILL.md # name must equal the directory name; keep each under ~5k tokens; global wins over workspace
hooks ~/Documents/Cline/Hooks or ~/.cline/hooks, one script per hook type; the kernel ships no adapter yet -> instruction-driven
source docs.cline.bot/customization/skills, docs.cline.bot/getting-started/config, verified 2026-11-02
```

¶ 6 — Other Harnesses

```text
rule any harness that reads a global instruction file and SKILL.md folders can host the kernel
install policy into its global instruction file with the merge markers, skills into its skill directory
no_skill_support -> append a skill index (name, description, path) to the policy; the agent reads SKILL.md on demand
```

¶ 7 — Runtime Capability Boundaries

capabilities:
  codex_and_claude: supplied_hook_adapters_translate_available_events
  post_write: no_automatic_reconciliation
  unobserved_write: reconciliation_only_on_express_operator_request
  antigravity_and_cline: instruction_driven_until_adapter_available
  independent_scan: explicit_operator_request_via_structure_tracker.py
  concurrency: limited_by_host_capacity_and_project_max_active_subagents
  absent_subagent_support: report_capability_limit_do_not_claim_delegated_execution
rule: hook_support_is_not_evidence_of_complete_write_interception
rule: scripts_do_not_choose_architecture_or_judge_implementation
rule: exclusive_write_ownership_includes_operational_files

¶ 8 — Departmental Compatibility and Behavioral Entry

contracts:
  layout: {{KERNEL_HOME}}/integration/installation/layout.tdsl
  loops: {{KERNEL_HOME}}/behavior/loops/catalog.tdsl
  SessionStart: existing_session_init_entrypoint_with_compact_context_snapshot
  SubagentStart: minimal_delegation_context_then_L04_cold_recovery_as_needed
  PreToolUse: existing_write_gates_and_once_per_session_policy_loading
  PostToolUse: no_automatic_reconciliation_or_commit
rule: host_without_hooks_uses_the_same_policy_and_skill_contracts
rule: deploy_all_departmental_dependencies_with_public_scripts
rule: hooks_never_classify_semantic_sufficiency_or_warm_cold_state
